{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "003S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$p : \\mathcal{S}\\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$p' : \\mathcal{S'}\\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$G : \\mathcal{S}\\to \\mathcal {S}'$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0006": "$G$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n\\Delta_G :\n\\mathcal{S}\n\\longrightarrow\n\\mathcal{S} \\times_{G, \\mathcal{S}', G} \\mathcal{S}\n$$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fully-faithful-diagonal-equivalence}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:98a9f25dd03e7dcaeee05e2121c3ae58bf1ed414cc3a7687157e6d59df5689a7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:93ca303386c5f4586cb4d705458ee96951151037508948ea74dbb21ace889252", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a category. Let <MATH_0002> and\n<MATH_0003> be categories fibred in groupoids.\nLet <MATH_0004> be a functor over <MATH_0005>.\nThen <MATH_0006> is fully faithful if and only if the diagonal\n<MATH_0007>\nis an equivalence.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3da1ba0344ee68ba1f01a199e0a2006d53e61d75a221462283303b35c876b43f", "unit_id": "tag:04Z7:statement"}
{"chapter": "categories", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "003S", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$(x, x', \\alpha)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\alpha : G(x) \\to G(x')$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{S}'_U$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Delta_G$", "MATH_0007": "$x$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{S}_U$", "MATH_0009": "$(x, x, \\text{id}_{G(x)})$", "MATH_0010": "$(x, x', \\alpha)$", "MATH_0011": "$\\Delta_G$", "MATH_0012": "$\\alpha = G(\\beta)$", "MATH_0013": "$\\beta : x \\to x'$", "MATH_0014": "$\\mathcal{S}_U$", "MATH_0015": "$\\Delta_G$", "MATH_0016": "$\\alpha$", "MATH_0017": "$\\beta : x \\to x'$", "MATH_0018": "$\\beta, \\beta' : x \\to x'$", "MATH_0019": "$G(\\beta), G(\\beta')$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-equivalence-fibred-categories}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:fefe4851c709947b24c2d28be5771dafcdf6cb2877fb610ee352144f86a4b85c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:6652259f05b5fcc0b206788377d28f50c68d891b902b370675806b5913d3813e", "source_text": "By\nLemma <REF_0001>\nit suffices to look at fibre categories over an object <MATH_0001> of <MATH_0002>.\nAn object of the right hand side is a triple <MATH_0003> where\n<MATH_0004> is a morphism in <MATH_0005>.\nThe functor <MATH_0006> maps the object <MATH_0007> of <MATH_0008>\nto the triple <MATH_0009>. Note that <MATH_0010>\nis in the essential image of <MATH_0011> if and only if <MATH_0012>\nfor some morphism <MATH_0013> in <MATH_0014> (details omitted).\nHence in order for <MATH_0015> to be an equivalence, every <MATH_0016> has to\nbe the image of a morphism <MATH_0017>, and also every two\ndistinct morphisms <MATH_0018> have to give distinct\nmorphisms <MATH_0019>. This proves the lemma.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:073e72412718b1b65de6199644503e0f98135e405cb6dcc8a1e75368724c7136", "unit_id": "tag:04Z7:proof"}
